     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day, which is roughly double the maximum daily dose. The usual maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg per day, and many institutions cap it at 2,000 mg per day. A dose this high risks lactic acidosis and serious GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a transcription error. Common intended doses would be 500 mg, 850 mg, or 1000 mg per dose.\n\nAlso, medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient's care. If you're acting for a physician, please have them enter the order or confirm the dose directly with them.\n\nIf you can tell me the intended dose, or confirm that a licensed prescriber has reviewed and approved it, I can enter it. I'd still recommend the prescriber confirm the dose and formulation before it's entered."
      }
     ],
